    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm looking at a 2022 F-150 with a slipping issue in the automatic transmission. I'm running some diagnostics and the tool is showing some really irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit. What are the most likely causes for these kinds of pressure fluctuations?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Irregular pressure spikes in an automatic transmission hydraulic circuit on a 2022 F-150 are a serious sign, and it's likely related to the internal workings of the transmission itself. These fluctuations can be caused by a faulty solenoid, a worn or clogged valve body, or issues with the transmission fluid level or quality. You should definitely have a professional mechanic look at it, as these issues can lead to more severe damage if ignored.",
      "source": "target",
